Sentinel Forge Study Workstation — Record & Pseudocode
What this is: the single-file web app (study-workstation.html) that runs as a Claude artifact. One HTML file holds three languages: HTML (structure), CSS (appearance), JavaScript (behavior). JSON is not a fourth language in the file — it is the data format the JavaScript uses to save to localStorage and to export/import sessions.
Artifact URL: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/f8cd1878-1dde-4b78-876a-2bbec1535b08 Working version: artifact Version 12 (2026-09-13) Broken version: Versions 10–11

1. Recovery record — what broke and why
Item
Detail
Symptom
Page loaded, but no tab buttons and no A1–G6 grid. Only the static Board frame showed.
Trigger
The edit that added the assistant's readSession tool (reading session JSON).
Root cause
That edit was pasted with curly "smart quotes" (” “) as JavaScript string delimiters in the saveNote and readSession tool definitions (script lines ~856–869). JavaScript only accepts straight quotes " ' and backticks.
Why everything vanished
A syntax error anywhere in a <script> block stops the whole block from running — the browser refuses to parse it at all. Everything the script would have built (tabs, grid cells, event listeners) never happened. Static HTML written by hand still rendered.
Fix
Replaced the curly quotes with straight quotes on those lines only. Zero other code changed.
Verified by
node --check on the extracted script (clean), then a browser reload showing tabs, grid, and the D3 sample card.
Data
localStorage keys gridindex-v1 and gridindex-set were never touched. Cards, library, notes, snapshots all intact.

Lesson for the gate: any code that passes through a word processor, chat window, or email can get its quotes "auto-corrected" into curly ones. Before publishing, run a syntax check (node --check file.js) or paste into an editor that highlights strings. Curly quotes show up as a different color than straight ones.

2. Padding audit (no code changed)
The box model in one breath
Every element is four nested boxes, inside → out: content → padding → border → margin. Padding is the space inside the border (it takes the background color). Margin is the space outside the border (transparent, pushes neighbors away). This file sets *{box-sizing:border-box}, which means a declared width already includes padding and border — the safe default.
Reading the shorthand
Padding shorthand goes clockwise from the top: top, right, bottom, left.
