Verdict
Nothing is broken and nothing needs changing for the page to work. The one real finding is inconsistency: values are 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 14, 16, 18 — not on any scale. Professional stylesheets usually pick a spacing scale (multiples of 4: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32) and store them as CSS variables like --sp-2:8px, the same way this file already does for colors (--accent, --line). That's a future cleanup, not a fix, and it belongs behind the gate.

3. Pseudocode — the whole app
FILE study-workstation.html
  <title>, <style> (CSS), HTML skeleton, <script> (JavaScript) — one file, no build step.

CONSTANTS
  KEY  = "gridindex-v1"              // localStorage key for all data
  COLS = A..G ; ROWS = 1..6          // 42 cells
  TABS = board, library, retrieve, assistant, study, session

DATA MODEL  (this is what the JSON looks like)
  STATE = {
    records:   [ card {id,title,body,coord "D3",zone GREEN|YELLOW|RED,cognitiveLoad 1-10,version,sourceDocId,parentId,createdAt,updatedAt} ],
    documents: [ doc {id,title,body,chapters[{title,pages[]}],createdAt,updatedAt} ],
    notes, journal, glossary: [ ... ],
    session:   snapshot | null,      // most recent snapshot
    snapshots: [ up to 20 snapshots ],
    log:       [ up to 100 {at,text} ]
  }
  SET = { autoRead, tint, zi (text-size index), readMode word|sentence|full, voice }
       // saved separately under key "gridindex-set"

PERSISTENCE
  load():  read KEY from localStorage → JSON.parse → merge over blank(); if empty, seed() a sample doc + card
  save():  JSON.stringify(STATE) → write to KEY        (called after every mutation)

BOOT  (runs once, bottom of the script, after all HTML exists)
  build the six tab buttons and wire click + arrow-key handling
  attach click listeners to every static button (Grid/List/Clear, Search, Save snapshot, Export, Import, tint, zoom, voice…)
  load()
  if a saved session has a selected cell → preselect it
  renderBoard(); applyTint(); applyZoom()
  if a saved session exists → insert "Welcome back" banner on Board

TAB SWITCHING  selectTab(id)
  mark chosen tab aria-selected, hide all panels except p-<id>
  call the panel's render function (renderBoard / renderLibrary / renderStudy / renderSession / renderAssistant)

BOARD
  renderBoard():
    grid view  → draw header row A..G, then for each row 1..6 draw 7 <button class=cell>
                 a cell shows its coord, the newest card's title, a count badge if >1, a zone dot
    list view  → all cards sorted by coord
    then renderCell()
  renderCell():  show cards stacked at the selected coord + "Add card here"
  cardItem():    one card with Edit / Branch / Find related / Delete (Delete offers Undo via toast)
  editCard():    inline form → validates coord A1–G6 and load 1–10 → upsertCard() → save()
  branchCard():  makes three child cards "— Define / — Effect / — Next" in the same cell
  findRelated(): same cell OR same petal OR ≥2 shared words (3+ letters)

LIBRARY
  addDoc(title, body):  splitChapters(body) → unshift into documents → save()
  splitChapters():      headings are lines starting with # / ## / ### or "Chapter N"; each chapter paginated 220 words/page
  file upload:          FileReader reads .txt/.md/.html; HTML is stripped to text first
  reader:               chapter/page navigation, read-aloud by word | sentence | full with follow-along highlight,
                        "Save page as note" / "Save page as card"

RETRIEVE  (the retrieve step of RAG — keyword only, no embeddings)
  tokens(str):  lowercase, split on non-alphanumerics, keep words > 2 letters
  retrieve(q):  for every record / document / note / journal / glossary item
                  score = number of distinct query words present in the item's text
                keep score > 0, sort by score desc then title, return top 12 with a 220-char snippet
  optional grounded answer: if toggle on → ask Claude with ONLY the hits as context, cite ids

STUDY
  three sub-tabs: notes / journal / glossary — each is a quick-add form + list with Delete+Undo

SESSION  (JSON in and out)
  Save snapshot:  {at, selectedId, selectedTitle, selectedCoord, query, recordCount, documentCount, logHead[5]}
                  → STATE.session and unshift into snapshots (cap 20)
  Export JSON:    bundle() = {records, documents, glossary, notes, journal, session, exportedAt}
                  → pretty-printed into a textarea, and downloaded if the platform allows
  Import JSON:    JSON.parse(pasted text) → for each of the five arrays, append items;
                  an id that already exists gets "-imp" appended → save() → re-render
  Delete JSON:    pick a snapshot to remove (with Undo)
  Activity log:   last 20 entries + list of saved snapshots

ASSISTANT  (Claude, tool-using, grounded in the user's own material)
  sendAsst(q):
    if no Claude access → explain and stop
    tools = [
      search(query)               → retrieve()
      createCard(title,body,coord)→ upsertCard()
      saveNote(title,body)        → addNote()
      readSession(limit)          → last N snapshots + last 10 log lines + current counts   ← the new tool
    ]
    system prompt: search first, answer only from hits, cite ids; call readSession before talking about past sessions
    reply → strip markdown → render as read-aloud units → optional auto-read → list of actions taken

ACCESSIBILITY SETTINGS
  reading tint (default / yellow / teal / cream), text size (5 steps via CSS zoom),
  read-aloud voice picker, read-by word/sentence/full, all remembered in SET

NOT IN THIS BUILD (named stubs, not silent)
  .docx/.pdf parsing · OneDrive/Drive import · Whisper dictation · vector search · cross-device sync

